<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta
    name="description"
    content="Privacy Policy for the Inkmoon iOS app."
  >
  <title>Inkmoon Privacy Policy</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --background: #f7f4ed;
      --card: #ffffff;
      --text: #292722;
      --secondary: #68645c;
      --accent: #735c3d;
      --border: #e4ded2;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 24px;
      background: var(--background);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI",
        Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    main {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 40px auto;
      padding: 40px;
      background: var(--card);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 18px;
      box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(45, 39, 30, 0.06);
    }

    h1 {
      margin-top: 0;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      font-size: 36px;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-top: 32px;
      font-size: 22px;
    }

    p {
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    a {
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    .updated {
      margin-bottom: 32px;
      font-size: 15px;
    }

    footer {
      margin-top: 40px;
      padding-top: 20px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      body {
        padding: 12px;
      }

      main {
        margin: 12px auto;
        padding: 24px;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 30px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <main>
    <header>
      <h1>Inkmoon Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: September 6, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <p>
        Inkmoon is designed to provide a private, offline-first experience.
        This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use
        the Inkmoon iOS app.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Data Collection</h2>
      <p>
        Inkmoon does not collect, store, sell, or share your personal data.
        We do not use advertising SDKs, analytics SDKs, or cross-app tracking
        technologies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Accounts</h2>
      <p>
        Inkmoon does not require registration or a user account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Local Data</h2>
      <p>
        Saved poems, reading preferences, language settings, appearance
        settings, and notification preferences are stored locally on your
        device.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some preferences and daily-poem information may be shared locally
        between Inkmoon and its Home Screen widgets using Apple’s App Group
        technology. This information is not sent to Inkmoon or its developer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Notifications</h2>
      <p>
        If you enable daily poem notifications, Inkmoon schedules them locally
        through Apple’s notification system. Inkmoon does not use remote push
        notifications and does not upload a device token.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>System Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        When you choose to share a poem, Inkmoon uses Apple’s system share
        sheet. Information is only sent to the service or person you select.
        The privacy practices of that selected service are governed by its own
        privacy policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        Inkmoon does not include third-party advertising, analytics, social
        networking, or user-tracking services.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Children’s Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Inkmoon does not knowingly collect personal information from children
        or any other users.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Data Deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Because Inkmoon does not maintain user accounts or remote user
        databases, there is no server-side personal data to delete. You can
        remove locally stored Inkmoon data by deleting the app from your
        device.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy if Inkmoon’s features or legal
        requirements change. The latest version will always be published on
        this page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, contact:
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:mimengtechcto@163.com">mimengtechcto@163.com</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer>
      © 2026 Inkmoon. All rights reserved.
    </footer>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
